Make Natron (RB-2.6) build with Qt6 / PySide6 / shiboken6 (-DNATRON_QT6=ON).

- CMake: require Qt6::Core5Compat (QRegExp) and do not inherit
  Py_LIMITED_API from an abi3 shiboken6: Natron embeds Python and
  uses the full C API.
- shiboken6: declare PyList/PyTuple custom types (no longer
  built in), give NATRON_BUILD_NUMBER a fallback for the header parser,
  and do not forward-declare QStringList (an alias in Qt6).
- Qt6 API: QMutexLocker is a template, QtConcurrent::run() takes the
  member function first, QDesktopWidget is gone (use QScreen),
  QString no longer takes QRegExp, QKeySequence[] returns
  QKeyCombination, key sequences are built with | instead of +,
  QStyleOption::init() -> initFrom(), viewOptions() ->
  initViewItemOption(), QTabletEvent pointer types moved to
  QPointingDevice, QApplication::globalStrut() removed.
- Include Qt headers before X11 headers (Status/Bool macros).
- qhttpserver: the "method" property has type HttpMethod.
- SequenceFileDialog: Qt::UpArrow is not a key, Ctrl+Up was meant.

Where the APIs differ, the Qt5 code path is kept behind QT_VERSION checks
(the Qt5 build itself has not been re-tested).
